    "skills": [
      {
        "name": "diagnose-the-bug",
        "scope": "shared",
        "source_kind": "global",
        "relative_path": "diagnose-the-bug",
        "description": "Reproduces a bug and explains its actual cause before anyone changes code.",
        "default_json_schema_name": null,
        "default_output_variable": null,
        "skill_md_content": "---\nname: diagnose-the-bug\ndescription: Reproduces a bug and explains its actual cause before anyone changes code.\n---\n\nReproduce and diagnose this bug before changing anything.\n\nReport: ${task_title}\n\n${task_body}\n\nFirst reproduce it, ideally with a failing test. Then find the actual cause -\nnot the first line that throws. Explain the mechanism in a couple of\nsentences: what the code assumed, and why that assumption is wrong here.\n\nWrite your diagnosis into an output block named `diagnosis`. Do not fix it yet.\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "fix-the-bug",
        "scope": "shared",
        "source_kind": "global",
        "relative_path": "fix-the-bug",
        "description": "Fixes a diagnosed bug at its cause, with a test that proves it.",
        "default_json_schema_name": null,
        "default_output_variable": null,
        "skill_md_content": "---\nname: fix-the-bug\ndescription: Fixes a diagnosed bug at its cause, with a test that proves it.\n---\n\nFix the bug described in this diagnosis:\n\n${diagnosis}\n\nReport: ${task_title}\n\nFix the cause, not the symptom. Keep the change as small as the cause allows.\nLeave behind a test that fails without your fix and passes with it.\n"
      }
    ],
